Modifications to the upstream code:
- Session TTL in seconds, with 0 meaning keep forever.
- No-restore entity types: selected types (e.g. SECRET) stay masked in responses.
- Multi-language analysis: results of several languages are unioned, with script-based language trimming.
- Exploded views for escaped text (JSON/Python-repr strings with literal \n, \", ...) so values inside them are found and replaced.
- Allowlist file plus structural and common-word filters that drop false-positive NER hits.
- Pattern-only indices: system/developer text is scanned with pattern recognizers only (no NER).
- Escape-aware replacer boundary: a literal escape sequence before a value no longer blocks the word boundary.
- Recognizer metadata (recognizer name/kind) carried through to results for auditing.
